From b24d0c7ff324c57c956cb10ecb6d41d5ca274ef1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jolyon Brown <jolyon@limilo.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 19:47:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 46/67] Accept integer null pointer constants in conditional
 expressions

Resolve pointer/zero operands in the parser, before the conditional's type
is chosen or its condition can be folded away. Convert an integer constant
expression with value zero to the other operand's pointer type, and apply
array/function decay when needed. Both existing IR lowering paths then
receive pointer operands.

Preserve integer-constant-expression provenance through constant folding
so ordinary and C const variables, floating arithmetic and pointer-to-int
casts cannot qualify merely because they fold to zero. Reject incompatible
numeric operands before optimisation can erase them. Fold logical negation
locally when evaluating a candidate null pointer constant.

Fixes nethack64 repro r51 in both operand orders.

Written by Codex; checked by Claude.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
